  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059980/assets/f579eb601605aa64fbc2c5bd1400a6c90ed974f15bfac81882b076ac93c443e1.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            The graph of $y=f(x)$ for $x\\le 1$ and the tangent line to the graph at the point $A(0,1)$ are shown above. \nEstimate the slope of the tangent using a forward difference approximation with step size $h=1.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The slope of the tangent is approximately equal to\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We use the forward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2032}(x)\u2248\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $x=0.$ The step size, in this case, is $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(0) & \u2248\\frac{f(0+1)-f(0)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(1)-f(0)}{1} \\\\  & ={e}^{1}+{1}^{2}+1-({e}^{0}+{0}^{2}+0) \\\\  & =e+2-1 \\\\  & =e+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
